{
  "an4.186:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.186 ",
  "an4.186:0.2": "19. Brahmins ",
  "an4.186:0.3": "Approach ",
  "an4.186:1.1": "Then one of the mendicants went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an4.186:1.2": "“Sir, what leads the world on? What drags it around? What arises and takes control?” ",
  "an4.186:2.1": "“Good, good, mendicant! ",
  "an4.186:2.2": "Your approach and eloquence are excellent, and it’s a good question. ",
  "an4.186:2.3": "For you asked: ",
  "an4.186:2.4": "‘What leads the world on? What drags it around? What arises and takes control?’” ",
  "an4.186:2.5": "“Yes, sir.” ",
  "an4.186:2.6": "“Mendicant, the mind leads the world on. The mind drags it around. When the mind arises, it takes control.” ",
  "an4.186:3.1": "Saying “Good, sir”, that monk approved and agreed with what the Buddha said. Then he asked another question: ",
  "an4.186:3.2": "“Sir, they speak of ‘a learned memorizer of the teaching’. ",
  "an4.186:3.3": "How is a learned memorizer of the teaching defined?” ",
  "an4.186:4.1": "“Good, good, mendicant! ",
  "an4.186:4.2": "Your approach and eloquence are excellent, and it’s a good question. … ",
  "an4.186:4.3": "",
  "an4.186:4.4": "",
  "an4.186:4.5": "",
  "an4.186:4.6": "",
  "an4.186:4.7": "I have taught many teachings: ",
  "an4.186:4.8": "statements, mixed prose & verse, discussions, verses, inspired exclamations, legends, stories of past lives, amazing stories, and elaborations. ",
  "a